sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Helpers used during one document upload
    accDescr: A client uploads a file with an API key. The service checks the key, checks type and size, spools the upload to disk, hashes and stores the original in MinIO, records a job, and later updates progress and finalizes the job. The client polls the job until it is terminal.
    autonumber
    participant Client
    participant Service as module-ttt
    participant H as base-tdb-helpers
    participant DB as SQLite
    participant S3 as MinIO
    Client->>Service: POST /v1/documents (Bearer API key)
    Service->>H: verify_api_key()
    H->>DB: look up hashed key in api_keys
    Service->>H: validate_file_type(), assert_content_length_within_cap()
    Service->>H: assert_spool_capacity(), write upload to spool
    Service->>H: compute_sha256(), upload_file(channel, hash)
    H-->>S3: put object (only if configured)
    Service->>H: job store insert() as QUEUED
    H->>DB: jobs row
    Service-->>Client: 202 Accepted, job_id
    Note over Service,H: worker: mark_ongoing(), update_progress(), finalize()
    Client->>Service: GET /v1/jobs/{job_id}
    Service->>H: get(job_id)
    Service-->>Client: state, stage, percent
